jobs.description:
We are looking for a Business Process Engineer for our customer in Kortenberg

Main tasks and responsibilities:

This role fits in the implementation and introduction of a new ERP and other systms for providing services to our customers. Togetherwith the European team, you will be analyzing the existing processes and defining the best practices and contribute to a succesfull roll-out and maintenance of the new ERP system and other systems.

Investigating and Analyzing current business processes, procedures and requirements and mapping them to SharePoint;

Documenting visualization of process and procedure flows;

Identification and assessment of potential risks in business processes and development of risk mitigation strategies;

Re-engineering and optimization of business processes and shaping new process policies;

Proposing smarter process management solutions for performance improvement and cost reduction;

Illustrating project descriptions, objectives, and measurements;

Collaboration with various stakeholders to identify potential for improvement;

Participate in and hold meetings to perform incremental agile software development framework when managing product development;

Support to evaluate and test administrative system changes to provide ongoing support to existing applications and implement new applications;

Staying updated with new software features and industry trends and educating people in the group.
Profile:

Several years of experience in business process analysis and optimization;

Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;

Ability to critically question processes;

Excellent communication and teamwork skills;

Accuracy and care in the analysis and documentation of processes;

Language skills in English mandatory.

Professional skills:

Excellent knowledge of Business Process Modeling, Business Process Reengineering and the related Management (BPM) Tools;

SharePoint: Knowledge in using SharePoint for mapping business requirements and managing document workflows;

Data Analysis Tools: Skills in using tools like Excel or Power BI for analyzing business data and visualizing process flows;

Nice to have:

Knowledge in SAP S/4HANA public cloud;

Agile Frameworks: Understanding and applying agile methodologies for software development and project management;

Software Testing: Experience in professional software testing and quality assurance;

Experience in Project Management and related Software is an advantage: Experience with tools like JIRA, Trello, or Microsoft Project for managing tasks and tracking progress;

Programming Languages: A basic understanding of programming languages like Python, Java, or C# can be advantageous for accurately assessing the feasibility of proposed changes.

Infratech is a part of the Netceed group , the market leader providing passive equipment solutions for the utilities sector: telecom, electricity, water & gas. Netceed currently presents more than 1000 highly specialized and motivated experts in EMEA and US, and have a turnover of over 1.000 million EUR. 

Infratech is growing and is looking for an expert in embedded software development to join their team in Thimister-Clermont. 

As an independent and motivated colleague, you have every opportunity to grow. If you think you would fit in with us, please apply for the position below.

As software engineer you draw up lists of requirements for all new products, as well as those for the evolution of existing products. In full collaboration with the project manager, you define a realistic development schedule. You will be responsible for the development of the software, with the quality procedures as a guideline. 

During this development, you prepare the necessary tests and trials, as well as the documentation. You works in coordination with your peers under the principles of the agile method. The position involves various projects but the main focus is on embedded development, integrated in a Linux environment. 

Development on microcontrollers (as well as support software for traditional PCs) is also possible. 

Your responsibilities will be as follows:

•  Analyse and review product requirements, discuss the technical feasibility and proposals ; 

•  Develop new software components or modify existing ones and take care of its integration ; 

•  Participate in peer code reviews ; 

•  Plan, define and perform unit testing ; 

•  Create or maintain technical documentation ; 

•  Solve defects reported in the defect tracking system ; 

•  Maintain existing applications ; 

•  Contact with the client for support and planification.

Profile 

•  You have a Bachelor or Master degree in Engineering or Computer Science; 

•  You have a strong knowledge or experience in C/C++;

•  You have knowledge or experience in Linux development (kernel modification, yocto, shell) ; 

•  You have knowledge or experience in embedded development; 

•  Will be considered as an asset: knowledge of LUA, TCL-TK, SQL, and familiarity with the following communication protocols: Modbus, IEC60870 & IEC61850 ; 

•  You achieve high-quality results through thoughtful analysis and planning; you are target driven and result oriented ; 

•  You are focused on quality, detail-minded and customer oriented; 

•  You are open for change and continuous learning ; 

•  You work autonomously ; 

•  You handle several projects at a time and juggle between tasks; 

•  You are fluent in French & have a working knowledge of English.

Our client is a leading international trading and supply chain organization with a long-established presence across Europe and a strong global footprint. Active in the distribution and trading of industrial and chemical products, the company combines commercial expertise, logistics capabilities, and financial strength to support international business operations.

Jobomschrijving

As Senior Accountant, you will play a key role in ensuring the accuracy of accounting operations, compliance, and financial reporting within an international business environment. Working closely with a Shared Service Center and stakeholders across Europe, your responsibilities will include:

• Managing monthly, quarterly, and annual closing activities, including accruals, reconciliations, and balance sheet reviews;
• Acting as the accounting reference point for the Belgian entity and overseeing the quality of accounting transactions processed by the Shared Service Center;
• Taking ownership of VAT compliance, tax-related reporting, and statutory obligations across multiple European jurisdictions;
• Coordinating annual audits and supporting the preparation of statutory financial statements;
• Partnering with business teams to provide accounting and tax guidance on commercial and operational activities;
• Ensuring compliance with local regulations, internal controls, and group accounting policies;
• Identifying opportunities to streamline processes, strengthen controls, and drive continuous improvement initiatives;
• Contributing to digitization and automation projects, including the adoption of innovative technologies and AI-driven solutions;

We are looking for a collaborative and flexible professional who enjoys taking ownership and working in a team-oriented environment. The ideal candidate combines technical accounting expertise with a strong process improvement mindset and has an interest in digital transformation and emerging technologies such as AI.

• Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field;
• Minimum 4 years of accounting experience within an international or B2B environment;
• Strong understanding of Belgian GAAP and VAT regulations;
• Experience with statutory accounting and external audits;
• Knowledge of SAP S/4HANA or SAP Hana is considered a strong asset;
• Fluent in English and French; Dutch is a plus;
• Analytical, detail-oriented, and process-minded;
• Comfortable working with multiple stakeholders in an international environment;
• Proactive, hands-on, and eager to contribute to continuous improvement initiatives;

Our client is a leading international organization dedicated to accelerating the transition towards a more sustainable future. Operating across Europe and beyond, it works with a wide network of partners to drive impactful initiatives and support long-term environmental and societal change.

Jobomschrijving

Reporting directly to the Head of Controlling, you will act as the reporting expert within the team and work closely with multiple Business Controllers across the organization.

Your responsibilities will include:

• Consolidating financial and management reporting from various business areas and ensuring the accuracy and consistency of financial data;
• Delivering consolidated reporting and analyses to support management decision-making;
• Reviewing financial data, performing reconciliations, and identifying key variances and trends;
• Acting as the point of reference for reporting standards, methodologies, and best practices;
• Driving automation and process improvement initiatives, with a strong focus on reporting efficiency and data quality;
• Leveraging Excel and reporting tools to optimize financial processes and reporting capabilities;
• Supporting budgeting, forecasting, and month-end reporting activities;
• Collaborating closely with Business Controllers and finance stakeholders across the organization.

• Bachelor's or Master's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a related field;
• Minimum 4 years of experience in financial reporting, consolidation, controlling, or audit;
• Advanced Excel skills are essential;
• Experience with reporting and automation tools is considered a strong asset;
• Fluent in English and French;
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
• Proactive, detail-oriented, and comfortable working with multiple stakeholders.
